# Input that must be REJECTED. The file the parse check exists for: a suite of
# valid molecules only proves what a parser accepts, never what it refuses,
# and a parser that accepts nonsense fails no valid-input test.
#
# Every line here is expected to produce a skipped record, not a molecule —
# except those NAMED `known-gap-*`, which record where that is not true yet. A
# gap is pinned rather than deleted so the corpus stays honest about what this
# parser really does, and so the test fails when the gap is closed and the
# marker needs removing.
#
# The marker is the entry's *name*, not a comment: a comment-scanning rule
# armed on the word appearing in this very header and swept up every line
# below it.

CC( unbalanced-open-paren
CC) unbalanced-close-paren
C1CC unclosed-ring-bond
[Xx] nonexistent-element
[C@@@H](C)(C)C invalid-chirality-marker
c1ccccc benzene-missing-closure

# KNOWN GAP #190: a run of bond symbols is silently collapsed, so each of
# these parses to the molecule its first symbol describes instead of failing.
C##C known-gap-doubled-triple-bond
C==C known-gap-doubled-double-bond
